#passage(("What are the evidences for the existence of Allah? The evidences for existence of Allah are different types; let's say four things. One, which is the religion, the Quran, the things that talks about Allah. The two more things: first is experience.", "Now we speak sometimes against the Christians and we say your religion is not true just because you have a personal experience; that doesn't mean your religion is true. But the reason we tell them that personal experience is not evidence: because other religions you can have personal experience, so it's a contradiction. But every religion on Earth has the experience of God; there's no contradictions there. Human beings as a species have an experience with God. Every single one of you probably have had an experience: you ask Allah for something that no one else knows about and you got it; you were in a difficult situation and Allah saved you when you ask him to help you. You have an experience with Allah. It's not just you but everyone, Muslim or non-Muslim: you have experiences with God, with the existence of the Creator. So then experience becomes an evidence.", "And then the last thing is intellect, for those who have intellect, because we know there's many people who don't have intellect, and because they don't have intellect they don't believe, or they outwardly say there is no God. But the truth is if you have intellect you believe.", "Then we have the intuitive thing that you're born with. Allah says when Allah took from Adam mankind, his progeny — he took mankind from Adam; this is before we are in this current life — and then Allah made us testify. Every human being Allah asked us: am I not your Lord? And we all said yes. You don't remember it, but the [fitrah] is there. When you're told about Allah, when you experience these things regarding Allah, this [fitrah] starts to awaken; deep down you feel, I know this is true, even though you don't remember the incident, but the effects of [fitrah] are there.", "Allah says in the [Quran]: you cannot change the creation of Allah, meaning every human being will have that. The Prophet: every child is born upon that. So that [fitrah] that we have as human beings, Allah says in the Quran he made us testify that he's Lord, and then we said we testify, and then Allah said to you: do not say on the day of judgment, we didn't know, no one told us that you're our Lord, no one told us that God exists. Allah is giving you the [fitrah], and that [fitrah] will make you recognize the existence of Allah.", "And even the disbelievers, they have studies, and these studies show that the [fitrah] is there. You have Oxford University conducting a study: 52 or 57 academics with the leading of Justin Barrett, who's an atheist, and they bring children, three years; they bring children from all different countries; they bring children from China, countries that don't even believe in God, and they conduct studies on these children, and then that atheist Justin Barett says: we, the atheist group of 50, we conclude that people innately believe in a Creator. This is in Oxford; this is not in my backyard, the Muslim backyard. So even the non-Muslims will admit to that. Dr Oliver Petrovich, he did a similar study with the Japanese children. There many many studies that those disbelieving people do, and it shows that the [fitrah] is there.", "So the [fitrah] is the evidence for God; the personal experience is the evidence for the existence of God; the Quran, where it speaks about Allah existence; and then the intellect, the common sense, the reasoning, for those who have the intellect and common sense and reasoning.", "We start with a very simple thing we all have as human beings, which is: we know that when something has a beginning it comes from something else; it comes from another source. That's why children always: Dad, what does this come from? What made it? Why are they saying that? The [fitrah] is within every human being to ask that question: where does everything come from? You look at the creation around you, and it's a very simple thing: you will have to come to the conclusion there's someone who made this.", "You see water coming down from the clouds. Is anyone here making the water come down from the clouds? No. But this water descends from the clouds; when it descends from the cloud it's one water, but when it goes in the soil it produces how many fruits, how many vegetables, how many different trees, how many different looks — same water. When that tree dies, do you do anything? It regrows by itself; it dies, comes back to life, just like when you die you'll be resurrected. That tree Allah has giving you an example, dying and resurrecting in front of you.", "These fruits that come, every single fruit is different from the other one; put a tomato under a microscope and they would be different. All of these fruits, the taste of these fruits, the colors of this fruit — is it one water, or how many water do we use? One water. We don't even do anything; it comes down by itself; all of these things grows. These are evidences that there is a Creator who is knowledgeable, wise, because we are using these things for our sustenance, we're using these things for our benefit, that has designed these things in that way in which has these effects.", "So you look at the ant: if you bring the ant and you want to see if the ant has a brain, how big is it going to be? Barely nothing. And look at the social behavior of ants: it is smarter than many human beings have met. The ants have a queen, have a hierarchy system; they have guards; they have prisons; they have punishments; they have armies; they protect the queen; they move food; they store food for long period of time; they have tactics and how they fight. Who told them this? If you look at this brain that you cannot even see, that is not even visible, how are they able to do this?", "There are things called termites; they're even smaller than ants; they exist in some parts of Africa, and they build these things which has internal ventilation systems that we're not able to build today. So who taught, who guided this creation? The one who created it. Allah is the one who made it and determined it to be the way it is. So isn't that a clear sign for anyone who has any intellect that Allah is a creator? Of course it is. Just looking at it is enough of an evidence.", "Also the fact: can something come from nothing? When we say nothing we mean the non-existence of everything; there's nothing in existence. I'll put it to you in an easy way: 0 plus 0 plus 0 equals what? It's zero. So it doesn't matter how many zeros you multiply, will always come to zero. You cannot have something from nothingness, but we have us and everything around us today. Allah says in the Quran: were they created out of nothing?", "Allah gives you possibilities now. You see this world, you want to deny and play games; okay, let's look at the possibilities. The universe came from nothing: can anything come from nothing? No. The universe created itself: can you create yourself? I heard some intelligent people before, when I was speaking to them, they said yes. You don't even exist; how are you going to create yourself when you don't exist? Did you create the heavens and the Earth?", "Subhan Allah, I tell you something very interesting: there isn't a single human being that we are aware of in human history that said I created the heavens. There are people who went to the extent of say we're God, but the one who said is God. So if you have something happening, an event happening, and only one person is saying I made this thing, no one else is saying I made it, do we believe him or no? Someone steal the cookie from the fridge and no one is admitting, and then our friend comes and says I stole the cookie, you going to believe him or no? You believe him. It's basic common sense to accept, because no one else has made that claim. So if we cannot create ourselves, then this universe that even atheist admit has a starting point has to come from something.", "So now when we look at these evidences, these are called the evidences for the existence of Allah. By the way, when we say intellect there's many many evidences; I'm just giving you a few examples. But why do you need to know this? First, to know yourself the evidences for why you believe in Allah; if you encounter an atheist on the road he tells you, you believe in God? You explain to him why you believe in Allah. And then your children. And to increase your faith as a person, why you believe in Allah yourself.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aqeedah (Creed) And Its Significance In Islam | AIM Conference 2024 NJ | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULnwXbVf_cM", ((1279, "21:19–22:20"), (1340, "22:20–23:09"), (1391, "23:11–23:27"), (1412, "23:32–24:33"), (1475, "24:35–25:22"), (1522, "25:22–26:20"), (1580, "26:20–26:34"), (1595, "26:35–27:08"), (1628, "27:08–27:46"), (1666, "27:46–28:21"), (1711, "28:31–29:20"), (1760, "29:20–30:05"), (1805, "30:05–30:53"), (1853, "30:53–31:31"), (1893, "31:33–32:39"), (1959, "32:39–33:06"),))
