#passage(("When you think about God — you cannot really visualize God, but when God is mentioned, the creator is mentioned, who do you think about? Is it a human being who's called Jesus who's walking Earth? Or is it a creator of the heavens and the earth we cannot conceive? Which one is it? This is the message of Islam. We say this message is innate to every human being. Prophet Muhammad told us that we are born with an innate disposition to recognize God, to know who God is, and to know our purpose in life. So, innately they're born believing in Allah. Definition of Allah in the Quran: Allah is uniquely one. Independent. Everything relies on God. God doesn't need anybody. He doesn't beget nor is born. Doesn't have children, parents, grandparents. And there is nothing like unto him. You're innately born there is a higher power that created the universe that is with this description I gave.", "It's a part of human nature. So, that is already mentioned in the Quran 1,400 years ago. Prophet told us every child is born upon fitra. Fitra is that innate disposition to know God. But then the prophet said, \"But then his father make him Christian, Jewish,\" or his parents change his religion.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Curious Couple Ask A Muslim To Explain World Suffering! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9AACeXB0A9Q", ((353, "5:53–6:50"), (433, "7:13–7:31"),))
