#passage(("You can look at certain tribes that were separated from the rest of the world; they still believed. So why do I need to prove something which is innately a part of my human nature? Just like there are axioms: I believe the belief in God is an axiomatic thing that you're born with, just like rationality is an axiomatic thing that you're born with, just like knowing causality is a real thing is an axiomatic thing that you're born with, intuitively knowing that you're choosing is an axiomatic thing that you're born with.", "This is something which is a fact: every Universal belief that we're born with, as human beings, as children, is true! Universal belief, that means all children are born with that belief. You saying some children have crazy stories, that's irrelevant. So when you have children from 20 different countries, like the study showed, from 20 different backgrounds, all saying the same thing essentially, it's an innate thing within human beings.", "So, for example, we have an innate thing of knowing causality, cause and effect; that's why you always see children saying where did this come from? Why? When? Where did they come from? Who did this? Who did that? So this causal belief, cause and effect, is an intuitive thing that is within human beings and it's true. Another thing that human beings have is they have a sense of even justice that we're born with, equality in a way, to say if you have two babies and you give a baby one cookie and you don't give it to the other baby, the other baby will get upset and will start crying! Because it recognises a sense of injustice that is innately put by the Creator within that baby.", "There's also another intuitive thing: that we exist. It's an axiomatic thing and intuitive knowledge within every human being that he exists. He's aware of his own self and there are surroundings around him. So I'm making the claim that all of these are intuitive beliefs that are Universal, and all of them are true. And one of them is the belief in God, because it's also an intuitive Universal belief that everyone has!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Challenges The Muslim Understanding Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tLX_TIbqsc4", ((485, "8:05–8:45"), (573, "9:33–9:56"), (600, "10:00–10:48"), (648, "10:48–11:04"),))
