#passage(("Every civilization that exists in human history, any history that we have of them, believed in some sort of a higher entity or a higher power. Give me one civilization that was strictly atheistic, that did not believe in a higher power. They believed in higher powers. The Chinese beliefs: they had different deities, but they still believed in higher powers. You're talking about things today. I'm saying back in history. Give me an example of a civilization — not a belief system, which is Taoism — a civilization or a group of people; they existed on a location that did not believe in any, that they were a purely atheists. You're not going to find them.", "By the way, even atheists disagree with you. Atheists, if you read the historical literature, they claim — which I disagree with them — but their claim is that polytheism started before monotheism. So, they claim that in the distant past, in these civilizations, they have polytheism. They were believing in different forms, different gods, different entities, etc., but they were polytheistic. But in summary, they believed in a higher entity. The Egyptians, the Chinese, everyone. They all believed in some form of higher entity.", "So, now you move the goalpost from that they didn't believe in a Creator, to that they believed in different forms of the Creator, which is irrational. It's irrational because it's different conceptions of God. So, you're saying if there are multiple ways to view something or do something, therefore that thing does not exist or is inaccurate. So, there is a thousand way of me to learn how to swim; that means you cannot learn how to swim because there's so many ways of how to swim? Or if there's so many people who describe me, Mohammed, so many people will describe me in different ways, that means I don't exist because there's so many different descriptions of me. That's in essence your argument.", "In fact, it goes against you, because if there are so many people describing an entity, that shows that this entity has existence, but they don't know the attributes or they're mistaken when it comes to the attribute of the entity. And by the way, they agree on many attributes, which shows that these things have evidence bearing because people believe in them.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Is Atheism Rational? Atheist Challenges Muslim! | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hFzWhMCQFn4", ((2466, "41:06–41:51"), (2516, "41:56–42:27"), (2574, "42:54–43:27"), (2614, "43:34–43:55"),))
