#passage(("If you're willing to accept the eternality of something, then why not God? If I'm willing to accept that something can be Eternal, then why would I attribute that eternality to something that is not a living and a conscious thing, rather than attributing to something that can actually initiate an action and a starting of this existence? Which one is more rational? So I'll say isn't there a bit of inconsistency there, if there is no evidence that the universe is eternal?", "Because the thing is, when you say is eternal, what do you mean? If you mean the universe we're living in: stars, galaxies, trees. Everything of these things I mentioned has a starting and ending point. None of it is eternal. If you mean the whole of the universe, the whole of the universe is a closed system, restricted system, because it's expanding. So that closed, restricted system, who closed it and restricted it? Why does it exist rather than not existing?", "We don't say there's nothing physical before the Big Bang, and the reason is because they say before the Big Bang our laws don't apply anymore. The equations show that our laws don't apply. If our laws don't apply, then the physical existence that we are aware of cannot exist. Therefore whatever exists before the Big Bang is something that is beyond the laws that we refer to. If something exists before the Big Bang, we say that thing brought the Big Bang into existence, cuz the Big Bang cannot expand by itself. So energy is not a conscious thing, cannot bring itself into existence. It requires an external entity.", "Consciousness is different, because Consciousness is related to the human being. I'm referring to material, for example the physical material. There's no consciousness there, because there's no human beings yet. I'm aware of the whole problem of Consciousness is a different thing in science, but I'm saying within the Big Bang, which is just physical material things, they're not conscious, just like this rocks or whatever it is. So they do not initiate decisions: we're going to expand right now, we're going to start existing. So they would require an external agency or external thing.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Examines The Muslim Belief In God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aymar_bEYMg", ((346, "5:46–6:17"), (379, "6:19–6:44"), (429, "7:09–7:49"), (483, "8:03–8:31"),))
// U ML310:69-126 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("I'll tell you my definition that I'm asking the question based upon: the absence of everything. The word \"nothing\" itself defines itself. It's no+thing. Just like the word triangle defines itself: tri = three angles. Nothing = no + thing. There's no other definitions of it. So nothing means the absence of everything.", "If there was always something that always existed that is not the universe, then it has to be something else. What we count as universe is that which energy cannot be created or destroyed within, atoms that are composed of what we refer to as the \"cosmos\". That's the universe.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Unintentionally Proves The Accuracy Of The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1tt_qknxI5I", ((275, "4:35–4:47"), (332, "5:32–5:45"),))
// U ML148:214-273 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("According to the scientific consensus today about the universe's beginning – you want to refer to it as the \"Big Bang\" or whatever – we know this universe has a starting point. Can it come from nothing? According to science and scientific laws – not only scientific laws, but rational laws – you cannot have something from nothing. There is no scientist today that says the universe came from absolute nothingness. Because they can't. Because every effect requires a cause.", "The universe that we have itself, it displays the attributes of the Creator. It displays the level of knowledge that we can never even comprehend within the laws of the universe. It displays the power, because the universe is made of atoms that have magnificent amounts of energy we cannot even comprehend.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Challenges The Muslim Stance On Evolution! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=daoNeH70SF0", ((720, "12:00–12:50"), (787, "13:07–13:18"),))
