#passage(("I understand your position, and it is the exact position the Quran describes people who don't believe. The idea of conjecture, the idea of I don't know, the idea of could be, could not be, I'm not sure. And when you've got that position, in reality you're not looking for the Truth, because you need to start from basic foundations of accepting or rejecting certain things in order for a person to move on.", "You are describing certain things in quantum mechanics. The most knowledgeable people in quantum mechanics, they say anyone who claims to know anything about quantum mechanics, he doesn't know. Because it's a baby science. So for you to come and claim that particles jump in and out of existence, this is a gross misunderstanding of how quantum mechanics works. How many interpretations of quantum mechanics are there? Do you know the Copenhagen interpretation, which is the basis of what you say, do you know that it is still probabilistic?", "We can probabilistically tell where the particles appear. Which shows that this is not randomly happening, which shows that there is external factors influencing these things that we are not yet familiar with. That does not mean they are by themselves popping in and out of existence. So do you know why you think they are by themselves pop in and out of existence? Because you start from a faulty purpose, which is that everything can be explained naturally.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Unintentionally Proves The Accuracy Of The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1tt_qknxI5I", ((436, "7:16–7:27"), (501, "8:21–8:56"), (542, "9:02–9:15"),))

