#passage(("There are many evidences for the Big Bang. It's not one. So, just to talk about one type of evidence and then to assume that therefore there is no Big Bang is disingenuous in a way.", "I would say Physics should bring you closer to God than it should bring you further. It should bring you closer, because you see the complexity of the Universe, the speed at which the Universe expands, all of these, like the distance between the Earth and the Sun, et cetera. There is a book called \"Six Numbers\". It's very good, very interesting on this topic.", "What I'm trying to say is that the Universe cannot exist without an external entity with a will and power that brings it into existence. You wouldn't doubt that someone made this phone or this table just by seeing the table; you don't have to see the maker. So we're saying similarly the Universe is self-evident for the existence of a higher power or something.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Jainism And The Concept Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uGkMScvv6oA", ((118, "1:58–2:41"), (182, "3:02–3:20"), (218, "3:38–4:25"),))
