#passage(("Can something come from absolute nothingness? Not only it doesn't make any sense, but it's impossible. 0+0+0 always = 0. The non-existence of everything and anything would always be the non-existence of everything and anything, because there's no energy, there's no matter, nothing can give rise to phenomena. There's no agency; nothing will ever happen. It will always be nothingness.", "A lot of agnostics, what they try to do, is not to take any position, and then we cannot have a conversation. So you obviously have to take stances. So it's either the universe has a starting point, or the universe does not have a starting point. If you're not an expert in a field, then a rational person would take the position of the experts. If the experts have a consensus on something, that there's a starting point of the universe today, referred to as the Big Bang, then of course I'm going to take the position of the experts, since I'm not a cosmologist myself. But if I don't want to take that, then there must be a reason why I don't want to take that position.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Calls Out Atheist Bluff To Avoid God's Existence! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8ZzMqxGlWfo", ((70, "1:10–1:33"), (169, "2:49–3:20"),))
// U ML008:141-250 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("No scientist says you can have something from nothing. Because science says there's a law in science called causality. Every effect requires a cause. When you appeal to science, science is against you there, because they all agree that you don't have something from nothing. If you can have something from nothing, you don't need science. Why? Because then the rain comes, it's from nothing. I don't need to conduct science to realize that there is wind, and there is steam and all of that. Nobody believes something comes from nothing. That's why science operates, because they disagree with that.", "Actually, Big Bang is not an explosion. It's a very quick expansion. There is a slight difference there.", "Energy and matter is not conscious. It's like your shirt. It doesn't move and act on its own. This rock is not going to stand up one day and start walking. And that's not maybe, maybe not. Just like saying, \"Oh, maybe your shirt came from nothing.\" No, it has to come from something.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Confident Atheist Challenges Muslim Then Gets Unexpected Answers! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HQZVh00S7XM", ((407, "6:47–7:19"), (494, "8:14–8:28"), (566, "9:26–9:59"),))
// U ML024:110-150 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("Now the difference is when we talk about created living beings like organisms or cells or whatever, these things are not conscious. Water is not conscious. The clouds are not conscious. So you ascribe human attributes to it when you say they do this or they do that. So I can say that makes no rational sense, because these cannot act on their own. They require a cause, they require a reason. Now the creator or God in our belief, or our belief of everybody who believes in God, is a rational entity that is eternal. Now without the entity you and me cannot exist.", "The amount of energy in the universe, the knowledge that you need to have, gravitational constants, atoms starts to form millions of years later, all of these stories like electromagnetic fields, orbits for planets and stars, you need knowledge you can't even comprehend.", "So, I'm saying by definition our existence must be a proof for existence of something beyond our comprehension as human beings. Because otherwise, you cannot have a universe. It cannot exist. So, I'm not here talking about fairy tales or anything. So, that would be very different now from talking about a rock doing something in its own, because it doesn't have a will. Doesn't have the ability. Doesn't have agency.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Confident Atheists Put To The Test By Muslim For Blindly Accepting Evolution! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qAOu953c5y8", ((270, "4:30–5:00"), (339, "5:39–5:51"), (352, "5:52–6:29"),))
